SWEET Bluetooth: VSC adapter for Apple multi-advertising (patch 0285, sprint-bt bt-proper 2026-11-10), default ON, boot-arg sweetbtvsc=0 turns it off with a log line. Spec docs/research/bt-vsc-adapter-spec.md. bluetoothd runs this phone on the BCM_4357 platform profile [bin docs/research/bt-platform-chipset-select.md s.1-3], which advertises only through Apple's vendor commands 0xfd48..0xfd4e (Create, Remove, SetParams, SetAdvData, SetScanRsp, Enable, UpdateAddress, layouts in that note s.6); the Pixel BCM4389 answers 0xfd48 with 0x01 [obs bt-bw2], so bluetoothd never advertises. The kernel UART driver is the controller as bluetoothd sees it: after the verified patchram download it reads the controller's own Broadcom multi-advertising capability (0xfd53, read-only, max_adv_inst >= 5 needed), then answers Create locally (ids 1..max-1) and translates the other six commands to the controller's 0xfd54 sub-ops 01-05 [src AOSP ble_advertiser_hci_interface.cc, docs/research/sprint-bt-fd48-firmware.md s.2a], rewriting the chip's replies to the Apple opcode. Set-Param tx_power is -7 dBm (AOSP default TX_POWER_MEDIUM, cited in the code). The ONLY controller commands it sends are 0xfd53 (once) and 0xfd54 sub-ops 01-05; no register or GPIO access is added. Both streams are framed into whole H4 packets (tx: commands held until complete, other packets forwarded as they arrive; rx: whole packets, local answers only between packets); a non-H4 byte, a length beyond the 2048-byte buffer or a uart rx error inside a packet stops the adapter for the boot (loud, pass-through). It refuses to start (BT GAP) if a diagnostic rewrite knob (sweetbtrw200b, sweetbtrw200c, sweetbtnopadv, sweetbtnopcf, sweetbtpubscan) is on, and every refusal, stray 0xfd54 reply and framing loss is a BT GAP row; BT VSC rows (first 16 in full, then powers of two) never print an address or payload byte; counters print when bluetoothd disconnects (new hook sweet_bt_uart_disc from sbt_disconnect in sweet_bt.c). Applies after 0277. Host test: tools/test_sweet_bt_vsc.sh. Not run on hardware. New hardware-write path (controller commands), unreviewed. Review fixes (docs/reviews/bt-proper-0285-review.md): Remove (0xfd49) of an instance that is not enabled is answered 00 locally with no chip command (as AOSP); sbu_vsc_cmd re-checks the adapter is on under the lock; the framing-loss rows print a stream offset, never a stream byte; sweet_bt_uart_disc runs before uart_busy is released.

